# The Python tool that the Windows packs of mistral.rs and llama.cpp use to read the import tables of their DLL and exe files,
# apart from the build tools. Each pack installs this file with build-tools.constraints in one
# `pip install --require-hashes --force-reinstall -r` call.
# pefile prunes the runtime DLLs that nothing imports (assert_engine_bundle.py --prune-runtime) and, in the mistral.rs pack,
# runs the import check of check_mistralrs_wheel.sh. It has no dependency and the build does not use it, so it changes no
# byte of the wheel. The ik and TEI packs do not read import tables and do not install it.
pefile==2024.8.26 \
    --hash=sha256:76f8b485dcd3b1bb8166f1128d395fa3d87af26360c2358fb75b80019b957c6f
